  "ingredients": [
    "2 large eggs",
    "1 tablespoon white sugar",
    "0.25 teaspoon salt",
    "1 cup sifted all-purpose flour",
    "1 cup milk",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "vegetable oil for frying",
    "confectioners' sugar for dusting"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/fUDJPbK2xEp4RlerFXKAz4O_uQE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-ingredients-4x3-2b3e6a3d52e54989a2cd2cd6c2a6c47a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beat eggs, sugar, and salt together in a large bowl. Add flour, milk, and vanilla extract; beat until smooth.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/viF7zQvPPL4f0ViJxyu8xigj-YA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-step-01-4x3-f522e0e86a0d4ceb91ee7c99fd9d393d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat about 2 inches of oil in a large, deep skillet to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Place a wire rack over paper towels.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the rosette iron in hot oil for 2 minutes. Lift the iron and let excess oil drain. Dip the iron in batter to 1/4 inch from the top of the iron, then dip the iron immediately into hot oil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1iBCyHQ6sWWQgssMjpePeen3SBM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-step-03-4-4x3-f375b981e14b40078c9d1fce7984a19c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fry rosette in hot oil until crisp and lightly golden, about 30 seconds.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/fDhe9r6g_GPD0N4Q6CCFlqNm5RU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-step-03-5-4x3-67abf6068a484197b11b56ba321d9af1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lift the iron out; tip upside down to drain. Use a fork to push rosette off the iron onto the prepared wire rack.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/4WdYmyzMSnYe-1f52j_noHpO1Xk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-step-04-4-4x3-f64457b1643d479f888ba3fd74ec7173.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reheat the iron in hot oil for 1 minute; cook remaining batter. Sprinkle rosettes with confectioners' sugar.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MEVeIexMo00JNX7SlrXMWPSMAPw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-step-04-6-4x3-fa76da43408c45de8b31ab0a79e832e7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Ud5SvLwoS7oKjGsIFI3k2DCenr0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/9809-rosettes-vat-beauty-4-4x3-dd043961d22f405196878f1066eaed05.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/9809/step_08.webp"
    }
